WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Mendel Palace, Candy needs your help.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:27.480
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:28.520
I'm Mike.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:29.700
I'm Sean.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:30.840
And I'm Joe.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.000
Mendel Palace, developed by a little company known as Game Freak.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.180
You guys know Game Freak?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.760
Never heard of them. Familiar, familiar.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.240
This is their debut game.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.800
This is their very first game.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.400
And it's not even just like, oh, well, who even was Game Freak back then.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.500
This is the Pokemon guys.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.540
This is the director of the game is Satoshi Tajiri.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.040
Yeah, Satoshi Tajiri is the director.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.580
He's the one who goes on to like, create Pokemon.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.640
And then you have Ken Shigemori is the artist who also does all the original art for the 151.

00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:09.140
I'm sure many of the Pokemon after that.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.300
Who can forget Shigs, right? Yeah.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.460
No, we call, that's what we call Shigeru Miyamoto.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:14.420
We call him Shiggy.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.240
I didn't say Shiggy. That's not what he said.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.800
Oh, what'd you say? Shug?

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.100
Shigs. Shigs, okay.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.620
Shiggy. Yeah, sure.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.360
That's the same thing, I think.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.580
I think we're having a semantics battle here.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:32.880
And then the composer, also Junuchi Masuda, who does all the music for the Pokemon games.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.760
So really, this is a Pokemon game, right?

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.000
It's the prequel.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:38.260
It seems to be.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.620
I mean, I can see it.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.060
Yeah, not even kidding.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:45.540
I think a lot of the sprites evoke Pokemon sprite work to me.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.200
Which makes sense, right?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.880
That's why we're saying that this is the team.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.260
And I like that it's the team, not just in name only, but also with the crew.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.740
So Mendo Pals, real fast, just want to get this out of the way, because I think it'll

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.440
be easier to explain now than in like a sequels and spinoff section.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.300
Mendo Pals originally came out in Japan as a game called Quinty.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.540
And they're basically the same game, like in game, everything's the same.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.200
The only thing different is the story.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.000
So while I'm explaining the American version, I might as well explain the Japanese version.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.860
The American version you play as the Bon Bon.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.200
Bon Bon, right?

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:33.240
Not Bon Bon. Bon Bon, who has to rescue his girlfriend Candy, who is trapped in her own dream.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:35.780
What? Is that last part necessary?

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:41.360
No, no, that's like a typical, that's like 100% like just a normal video game.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.380
It's Sleeping Beauty. Yeah, I guess so.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.060
Like, right, the Candy part is like, you know, that's her name and whatever.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:51.140
But like the rest of it, too ridiculous.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.480
I mean, I'll be honest, I played a significant amount of this game.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.800
I know absolutely nothing about any of this story.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.600
So I don't have much to add here.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.500
You can play this game for 10 levels and not know that there is a story.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.880
Yeah, that's true. Actually, yeah, you just, you do get just thrown into it.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.680
The Japanese version, the protagonist name is not Bon Bon.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:13.900
It is Carden.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.900
His girlfriend is Jenny.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.660
And she has been kidnapped by Carden's jealous younger sister, Quinty.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.480
That is very important to say.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:35.620
Um, uh, the one thing that I kept like running into when I was at least reading about this game, because I'm not gonna, you know, get firsthand sources.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:43.120
It's all secondhand for me, was like just how annoyed everyone was with how cute the game was.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.680
Is it, were you running into this too?

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:46.840
I wasn't.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.600
Uh, I was, I was very pleased with how cute the game was.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.040
Oh, no, no, no. Like, I was.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.520
No, I know, I know. But I just, I'm surprised that that was the, uh.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.300
Yeah, but it's just funny that like everything I was reading was just like, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.560
But can you cut out all the cute stuff?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:07.960
And it sounds like the story is really leaning into that cute stuff in a way that we wouldn't think about it otherwise.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:17.620
I don't know. It's funny because like, I can, I can understand that if it's like an existing property that it's like, oh, it's gotten really cute now.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.140
It's like, oh yeah, it's like, uh, Pokemon now.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.220
They're too cute. They used to be like fierce or whatever.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.240
I get that if someone, you know, I don't think that's true.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:29.760
But like, if someone had, if that's the direction that they went with this is like, this is just a cute game.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.300
Like, like that's what they made.

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.140
They'd be like, ah, I don't make this cute.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.260
It's like, that's what it is.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.280
It's like already is.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.740
It's like saying like, ah, Kirby should be edgier.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.480
Well, he is in, uh, in Japan.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.080
He doesn't smile on any of the box arts.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.320
Do you know about that?

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:45.460
I didn't know it.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:51.640
If you look up any Kirby video games box art in the North American box, he's smiling.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.520
